<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ColourPrimaries 2 (Unspecified): a MEMBER of the sub-class that is
  NON-CONFORMING, and the fixture that keeps those two axes apart.

  Clause 8.7.1.1: "When ColourPrimaries is equal to 2 (Unspecified), the
  cicpType shall carry the custom chromaticity extension of 10.3", and NOTE 2
  states the consequence - "An HDR ColorSpace Profile whose ColourPrimaries is
  2 without that extension present is non-conforming, because 8.7.1.2 c)
  would then have no chromaticities to compute the matrix from."
  Non-conforming, note, not a non-member: it is an HDR ColorSpace Profile that
  is broken, the way a profile missing a required tag is.  So
  icGetHdrProfileInfo() reports icHdrProfileConforming and Validate() reports
  NonCompliant, and a build that conflates the two fails this fixture.

  BLOCKED, AND THE FIXTURE RECORDS WHY.  ICC.1:2022 10.3 Table 32 is twelve
  bytes ending at VideoFullRangeFlag - there is no chromaticity array in the
  published clause - and the amendment that appends one, the CICP Unspecified
  Primaries Amendment Proposal v2 named in this amendment's normative
  references, is not available to this tree.  Its byte layout, presence
  signalling, entry count and number encoding are all unknown, so CIccTagCicp
  reads twelve bytes and cannot distinguish a profile carrying the extension
  from one omitting it.  Both are refused, and the diagnostic says so, so that
  a reader whose profile does carry one can see the finding is this build's
  limitation rather than their file's defect.

  WHAT THIS FIXTURE USED TO BE.  Under clause 8.10.1, ColourPrimaries 2
  required the matrix column tags to be present and used directly as the
  RGB-to-PCSXYZ matrix, and this was the POSITIVE of a pair whose negative,
  HdrCicp2NoColumns, omitted them.  A ColorSpace profile has no matrix column
  tags, 8.7.1.1 NOTE 2 now takes the white point from the extension rather
  than from mediaWhitePointTag, and the two fixtures had collapsed into the
  same test - so HdrCicp2NoColumns is DELETED and its colorant tags are gone
  from here.

  WHEN v2 ARRIVES this fixture is the first thing to revisit: it should carry
  the extension and return to being a positive, with a new negative alongside
  it for the profile that omits one.

  EXPECTED CLASSIFICATION is icHdrProfileConforming; expected validation
  verdict is `noncompliant`.
-->
<IccProfile>
  <Header>
    <PreferredCMMType>ICCD</PreferredCMMType>
    <ProfileVersion>4.50</ProfileVersion>
    <ProfileDeviceClass>spac</ProfileDeviceClass>
    <DataColourSpace>RGB </DataColourSpace>
    <PCS>XYZ </PCS>
    <CreationDateTime>2026-08-05T00:00:00</CreationDateTime>
    <ProfileFlags EmbeddedInFile="false" UseWithEmbeddedDataOnly="false"/>
    <DeviceAttributes ReflectiveOrTransparency="reflective" GlossyOrMatte="glossy" MediaPolarity="positive" MediaColour="colour"/>
    <RenderingIntent>Relative Colorimetric</RenderingIntent>
    <PCSIlluminant>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </PCSIlluminant>
    <ProfileCreator>ICCD</ProfileCreator>
  </Header>
  <Tags>
    <!-- Standard Bradford D65 to D50 adaptation. -->
    <chromaticAdaptationTag> <s15Fixed16ArrayType>
      <Array>
        1.047882  0.022919 -0.050201
        0.029587  0.990479 -0.017059
       -0.009232  0.015076  0.751678
      </Array>
    </s15Fixed16ArrayType> </chromaticAdaptationTag>

    <mediaWhitePointTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </mediaWhitePointTag>

    <cicpTag> <cicpType>
      <cicpFields ColorPrimaries="2" TransferCharacteristics="16" MatrixCoefficients="0" VideoFullRangeFlag="1"/>
    </cicpType> </cicpTag>

    <!-- The same rule the cicpTag exercises, now in the metadataTag. The
         registry says a primaries code of 2 in CLL or CCV "means that the
         primaries are defined by tags required by [a] three component
         matrix-based display profile containing this metadata", and the ICC
         HDR Display registration of 2026-06-24 says of DCV that "a primaries
         value of 2 has the same meaning as in the cicpTag".

         This profile is the one shape where that can actually be satisfied: it
         declares ColourPrimaries 2, so 8.7.1.1 requires the matrix column tags
         to be present, and they are what the code resolves against. In any
         other conforming HDR ColorSpace Profile the same entry has nothing to resolve
         against, because the revision removes those tags - see HDR-18. -->
    <metaDataTag> <dictType>
      <DictEntry Name="CLL" Value="600.0 300.0 2"/>
    </dictType> </metaDataTag>

    <!-- There are no TRC tags and no matrix column tags, and under the
         23-09-2026 revision that is not a prohibition being obeyed - it is
         what a ColorSpace profile IS. 8.7 never defines either set for this
         class, so, in the revision's words, "there is nothing for this
         amendment to prohibit". The transfer comes from the cicpTag's
         TransferCharacteristics field and the primaries from its
         ColourPrimaries field; 8.7.1.1 says the cicpTag "is the only tag that
         can convey either".

         The AToB0Tag/BToA0Tag pair below is required by 8.7 of every
         ColorSpace profile, which 8.7.1.5 leans on rather than restates -
         "both already unconditionally required of every ColorSpace profile by
         8.7" - and it is what gives a legacy CMM a rendering path. Identity B
         curves: these fixtures exercise classification and the tone-mapping
         chain, not the bake's accuracy. -->

    <AToB0Tag> <lutAtoBType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutAtoBType> </AToB0Tag>

    <BToA0Tag> <lutBtoAType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutBtoAType> </BToA0Tag>

    <profileDescriptionTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[iccDEV HDR ColorSpace Profile, cicp ColourPrimaries 2: non-conforming without the 10.3 extension]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </profileDescriptionTag>

    <copyrightTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[Copyright (C) 2026 The International Color Consortium. Generated fixture, no measured data.]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </copyrightTag>
  </Tags>
</IccProfile>
